# Confluence Page

**Use for:** durable documentation — runbooks, architecture notes, how-tos,
decision records, onboarding, and project wiki pages.

**Do not use for:** tracker work (→ `jira` plugin), one-line chat replies, or
pasting secrets.

## Create

Follow `confluence-create`. Prefer a parent page when the space already has a
clear tree. Title should name the topic outcome, not a temporary scratch
label.

## Body

Required shape from `confluence-structure`:

1. **Overview** — why / audience / outcome
2. **H2 sections** — one job each, stable names for later section updates

## Diagrams

When the page needs an architecture or workflow figure, follow
`confluence-diagrams` (author with `drawio-author`, then attach).

## Done

A page create or rewrite is done when Overview + sections are published, the
browse URL is returned, and any requested diagrams are attached. Product code
is out of scope unless the user added an explicit implement verb.
